  "Question": "Simplify \\(x(2x-3)-2x(x-1)\\), and find its value when \\(x=5\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "-5",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(x(2x-3)-2x(x-1)=2x^2-3x-2x^2+2x=-x\\). When \\(x=5\\), the value is \\(-5\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Factor out x\n\nBoth terms have a factor \\(x\\), so factor it out to simplify one bracket:\n\\[\nx(2x-3)-2x(x-1)=x\\bigl[(2x-3)-2(x-1)\\bigr].\n\\]\nThe bracket equals \\(2x-3-2x+2=-1\\). Thus the expression is \\(-x\\), and when \\(x=5\\), its value is \\(-5\\).",
